# Project Conventions

## Stack

- TypeScript, React, Vite
- Tailwind CSS for styling
- ESLint + Prettier for linting/formatting
- npm as the package manager

## Coding conventions

- Prefer functional components and hooks over class components.
- Keep components small and colocate related files (component + styles + test)
  under `src/components/<ComponentName>/`.
- Use named exports, not default exports, except for page-level components.
- Type all component props explicitly; avoid `any`.
- Prefer Tailwind utility classes over custom CSS unless a pattern repeats 3+
  times, in which case extract a component or a `@apply` class.

## Git conventions

- All commits follow [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/):
  `type(scope): short description`
  - Common types: `feat`, `fix`, `chore`, `docs`, `refactor`, `test`
  - Example: `feat(setup): add project scaffolding and tooling`
- Keep commits scoped to a single logical change.

## AI assistant behavior

- When asked to critique a file, give concrete, actionable feedback (not just
  praise) and prefer the smallest change that meaningfully improves it.
- Ask before adding new dependencies.
- Match the existing code style rather than introducing a new pattern.
